{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Decomposition (cluster T1, 2026-11-19 PST). Children in landing order, each its own Gerrit change:\n1. calcite-cursed-lovebird — ADR 0125 records the decision and supersedes ADR 0049's pinning (and the ADR 0104 decision-3 dependency). Epic AC 1.\n2. unequaled-sincere-firefly — adds `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` (entries `<env_id> <key-type> <base64> [comment]`, env `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS`, `mechanism-ok` marker naming this epic), the `untrusted` verdict and `signing_key` report, and sets the 3 current keys in the MCP deployment (compose `mcp` service + autodeploy `mcp_run_new`). Epic AC 4 and 5.\n3. notorious-deadsmooth-rattail — validity-only default; signing, health and `verify-opcert` stop reading the pin file. Epic AC 3.\n4. prosaic-visionary-basilisk — deletes `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `attest/trusted_env.py` and `rebar trusted-env`. Epic AC 2.\n5. waterish-aquamarine-bug — docs and runbooks, including `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`.\nEpic AC 6 (make verify + Gerrit votes) is met per child.\n\nOrder change versus the requested \"core → config\" sequence: the config setting and the MCP deployment list land together BEFORE the core change. If the core change landed first, the live MCP server would run validity-only (no list) between the two deploys. With this order the server always has either the pin file or its own list.\n\nDesign choices made within scope (one line each):\n- Trust-list entries bind a key to an environment id, mirroring the operator's env→keys listing; a listed key presented under a different principal is `untrusted`.\n- `verify.require_environment` keeps its meaning and now requires a trust list, since a principal alone is a self-claim; without one it refuses (`foreign_key`), preserving today's \"no self-certification under enforcement\" property.\n- Keys in the list carry no eras; removing a key untrusts every certificate it signed.\n- Review-bot and developer clones get no list and become validity-only, per the default."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795112782690480170,"uuid":"ce5f1610-086f-4374-a422-fdaf89952d6a"}